  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "v5.8.14 - on SpawnDev.ILGPU 5.4.26. The opt-in int8-activation mode (env GGUF_INT8_ACT=1 or FusedDequantMatMul.Int8ActGemv; off by default, CUDA) is much faster at prefill: qwen3:1.7b Q4_K_M on an RTX 4070 prefills a 1,830-token prompt at ~14.1k tok/s against the default's ~9.9k (+42%), and decodes at ~261 / ~243 tok/s (default ~237 / ~222). New: the int8 Q4_K GEMM reads the GGUF rows directly (no unpack pass), the norm and SwiGLU write the int8 activations, gate | up applies SwiGLU in its epilogue, and F16 weights take one f16 GEMM as Ollama does. Measured cost of the mode against the default: KL 5.5e-3 (decode), 3.9e-3 (prefill), perplexity +1.1%. The default fp32 path is unchanged. See CHANGELOG.md.",
